⚠ Corbanu Terminal is using the non-admin Windows sandbox. It blocks sandboxed
  commands from creating, changing, deleting or moving files outside the folders
  they may write to, except in places marked low-integrity (such as
  AppData\LocalLow) and in folders another non-admin sandbox session is using.
  It does not stop commands from reading your files, its network block is only
  proxy and tool settings that a program can ignore, and a few ways of starting
  programs get partly outside it. Commands running at the same time in different
  projects aren't kept apart: one can borrow another's access and write in its
  folders (the default sandbox doesn't prevent this yet either), so avoid
  running commands in several projects at once. Switch to the default sandbox
  (one-time Administrator setup) by running /setup-default-sandbox, or set
  `sandbox = "elevated"` under `[windows]` in config.toml. Learn more:
  https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/blob/main/docs/sandbox.md#windows-non-admin-sandbox
